{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/swiduxrelationcodec"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxRelationCodec","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Why a converter can’t just rebuild its children","anchor":"Why-a-converter-cant-just-rebuild-its-children","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The obvious ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update(from:)"},{"text":" body — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self.chapters = domain.chapters.map { ChapterModel(from: $0) }"},{"text":" — is a row leak. A relationship’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleteRule"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fires when the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"parent","type":"text"}]},{"text":" is deleted, never when a child is dropped from the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relationship, so the previously-related rows are detached rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"removed: they stay in the store with no owner, and nothing ever collects"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. Every save of the parent leaves another full copy of its children"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behind, the store grows for the life of the app, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toDomain()"},{"type":"text","text":" — which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only walks the current relationship — shows nothing wrong."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"So the write-back reconciles by ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead: rows whose identity survives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are updated in place, new identities are inserted, and identities that are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gone are deleted outright.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Identity-not-row-identity","level":2,"text":"Identity, not row identity","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconciling in place also keeps "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"type":"text","text":" stable across a save."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That matters beyond tidiness: a rebuilt child is a delete plus an insert, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under CloudKit mirroring every parent edit re-uploads its whole subtree, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every one of those writes a history transaction that a remote-change tick"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then has to resolve."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Duplicates-are-kept-as-everywhere-else","level":2,"text":"Duplicates are kept, as everywhere else","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" emits no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Attribute(.unique)"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" (CloudKit forbids unique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constraints), so several related rows may legitimately share one identity."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are all updated and all kept, matching "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB"},{"type":"text","text":": converging every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matching row is safe, while picking one survivor is not — two devices pick"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different rows, each tombstones the other’s, and both are lost."}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec\/reconcile(_:with:in:)-34utk","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec\/reconcile(_:with:in:)-9zflx"],"generated":true}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxRelationCodec","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence0A13RelationCodecO","title":"SwiduxRelationCodec","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxRelationCodec","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/SwiduxRelationCodec"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconciles a generated model’s "},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" properties against the domain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value being written. Not meant to be called directly."}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"title":"EntityDB","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads and writes any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","kind":"symbol","role"